    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "How often",
     "texto": [
      "**まいにち** (every day), **いつも** (always), **よく** (often), **ときどき** (sometimes). They go before the verb.",
      "**あまり** (not much) and **ぜんぜん** (not at all, never) take a verb in the **negative**: **あまり しません** (I don't do it much), **ぜんぜん みません** (I never watch it)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Where and with whom",
     "texto": [
      "**で** marks the place where an action **is done**: **うち で ほん を よみます** (I read a book at home). Don't confuse it with **に**, which marks where something **is**.",
      "**と** with a person means «with»: **ともだち と** (with a friend).",
      "**します** is «to do»: **スポーツ を します** (to do sport), **テニス を します** (to play tennis)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
